 "description": "HVACR Survival is about the reality of life in the trade. I’m Rick Dirmeyer, and I’ve spent over 30 years as a service tech navigating the highs and lows of commercial and industrial refrigeration.\n\nI’m here to share the practical, real-world diagnostics that manuals often leave out—from troubleshooting Stoelting ice cream machines to servicing chillers, boilers, and industrial generators. This isn't about being a \"super tech\"; it’s about the grit, the mistakes, and the hard-won lessons learned from three decades on the front lines.\n\nWhat we tackle together:\n🛠️ Commercial Refrigeration: Soft serve (Stoelting/Taylor), rack systems, reach-ins.\n❄️ Industrial HVAC: Chillers, geothermal, and Make-up Air Units (MAU).\n⚡ Power Systems: Generator service and electrical troubleshooting.\n🧰 Tool Reviews: Honest field-testing of gear from TruTech Tools and Fluke.\n\nSupport the channel:\n👉 Save 6% at TruTech Tools with code: SURVIVAL\n🔗 Tools: https://kit.co/hvacrsurvival\n📬 hvacrsurvival@gmail.com\n",
